    <string name="intro_lore">That year, the light began to go missing.\nNot nightfall — night passes. The light forgot how to stay on the ground.\nCities dimmed one lamp at a time, roads lost their edges, maps turned back into blank paper.\n\nThen people found out: light returns only where someone has walked.</string>
    <string name="intro_tagline">Light won\'t return on its own. You walk it back.</string>
